==Finnish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|fi|jompi kumpi}}

===Etymology===
{{dvandva|fi|jompi|kumpi}}, which are related to the stems {{m|fi|joka|jo-}} and {{m|fi|kuka|ku-}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p|jompi-kumpi}}

===Determiner===
{{head|fi|determiner}}

# {{lb|fi|indefinite}} [[one]], [[either]] of two
#: {{ux|fi|'''Jommankumman''' on pakko mennä.|'''One of the two''' [of us] has to go.}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|fi|pronoun|cat2=indefinite pronouns}}

# {{lb|fi|indefinite}} [[either]] [[one]] of two
#: {{ux|fi|'''Jompikumpi''' teistä valehtelee.|'''Either one''' of you lies.}}

====Usage notes====
* The pronoun is generally treated as singular, with the exception of the {{gl|imperative}} mode.
:: {{ux|fi|jompikumpi tul'''ee'''|one of the two comes}}
:: {{ux|fi|tul'''kaa''' jompikumpi|come, either one of you two}}
* {{m|fi||jompikumpi}} also has plural forms, which are used e.g. with words that are only used in the plural: {{m|fi|jommatkummat [[häät]]||either one of the weddings}}.

====Declension====
Both parts are declined.
